#### Timing rules for financial information

| Document | Freshness requirement |
|---|---|
| Owner financial statement (SBA Form 413 or Lender's equivalent) | Signed and dated **within 90 days** of submission to SBA |
| Business financial statements | Dated **within 120 days** of submission to SBA |
| Interim financial statements | Dated **within 120 days prior** to submission to SBA |
| Seller's financial statements (business purchase) | Last 3 complete fiscal years (or years in business if fewer); dated and signed or certified by the seller **within 120 days** prior to submission |
| Seller's interim statements | No older than **120 days** from submission; dated and signed or certified |

#### Business financials

The Lender must obtain tax transcripts (Section A, Ch. 5, Para. B) and either **business financial statements or tax returns for the last 3 years**, plus **interim statements**, for the Applicant **and any affiliates**:

1. Year-end balance sheets for the last 3 years, with a **detailed debt schedule**;
2. Year-end profit and loss statements for the last 3 years;
3. Interim balance sheet (with detailed debt schedule) and interim P&L.

**Start-ups, new businesses, and other projection-based applications** must include **detailed projections with supporting assumptions** showing **debt service coverage of 1.15 or greater within 2 years from loan funding**, or for construction projects, **within 2 years from the end of construction**.

#### If proceeds will purchase real estate

- **Appraisal** meeting Appendix 19's commercial real estate appraisal requirements;
- Copy of the **signed purchase agreement**;
- Lender's **environmental questionnaire**, if applicable (Section A, Ch. 5, Para. E);
- **Cost breakdown** where improvements are included (submitted for non-delegated loans).

#### If proceeds will purchase an existing business

- Copy of the **buy-sell or purchase and sale agreement**;
- **Business valuation** meeting Appendix 15 Para. C.1.a requirements;
- **Pro forma balance sheet** for the business being purchased as of the date of transfer;
- **Seller's financial statements** and **interim statements** (timing above);
- All documentation required in Appendix 15, Para. D.

If the seller's financial statements are **not available**, the seller must provide an **alternate source of verifying revenues**, and the Lender's credit analysis must discuss **why** the statements are unavailable and **how** the Lender verified business revenue.

> **Watch out:** Owner financial statements have a shorter shelf life (90 days) than business financials (120 days). A deal that sits in underwriting can easily outlive a personal financial statement.
